WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.170
The characteristics that make embedded systems operate

2
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.550
efficiently are also a security risk.

3
00:00:12.029 --> 00:00:14.770
Embedded systems are often used to control something

4
00:00:14.779 --> 00:00:17.209
physical such as a valve for water,

5
00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:19.040
steam or even oil.

6
00:00:19.049 --> 00:00:21.989
These devices have a limited instruction set and are

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.190
often hard coded or permanently written to a memory chip

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.250
for ease of operating the mechanical parts.

9
00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:30.989
The embedded system is often connected to a corporate

10
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.619
network since and may operate using the TCP/IP protocol.

11
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.169
Yes, the same protocol that runs all over the internet.

12
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:40.250
Therefore,

13
00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:43.840
it is feasible for anyone anywhere on the internet to control the

14
00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:47.650
opening and closing of a valve when the networks are fully connected.

15
00:00:48.159 --> 00:00:52.450
This is the primary reason for segmentation of these systems on a network.

16
00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.689
If these are segmented properly,

17
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.069
a compromised corporate network will not be able to

18
00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.369
access the physical controls on the embedded systems.

19
00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:04.680
The other side of the embedded systems which also applies

20
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.309
to IOT devices is the general lack of system updates.

21
00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:10.319
When a new vulnerability is found

22
00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.029
in the case of most embedded systems with the programming directly on the chips,

23
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.120
it would require physical replacement of the chip to patch the vulnerability

24
00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:20.790
for many systems.

25
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.269
It may not be cost effective to have someone visit each one to

26
00:01:24.279 --> 00:01:28.389
replace a chip or manually connect to the chip to reprogram it.

27
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.330
We buy all these internet connected things because of the convenience

28
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:37.620
cameras, light bulbs, speakers, refrigerators, et cetera,

29
00:01:37.629 --> 00:01:40.660
all bring some sort of convenience to our lives.

30
00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.660
But they also introduce risk.

31
00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.519
While the reputable mainstream brands will

32
00:01:45.529 --> 00:01:47.550
likely provide updates to their devices.

33
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:49.559
When a new vulnerability is discovered,

34
00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.970
many of the smaller companies simply don't plan to do that

35
00:01:53.059 --> 00:01:56.000
as they seek to control the costs of a device.

36
00:01:56.139 --> 00:02:00.440
These devices when connected to a corporate network can be an easy

37
00:02:00.449 --> 00:02:04.550
internet connected doorway for a cyber criminal to access a corporate network.

38
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.830
If these devices are properly segmented or separated on

39
00:02:08.839 --> 00:02:12.050
the network from corporate servers and other corporate networking,

40
00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:16.490
a compromise on an IOT device or a compromised embedded system

41
00:02:16.539 --> 00:02:20.100
will not be able to access those corporate data and systems.